      "writtenOn": "2026-06-05T17:49:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**EC Checksum Validation is Vulnerable to USB Padding** In `ec_comm.cc`, `VerifyResponseChecksum` calculates the checksum across the entire received USB payload:\n\n```c\nresp_buf.resize(actual_res.value());\nif (!VerifyResponseChecksum(resp_buf)) { ... }\n\n```\n\nUSB bulk endpoints frequently pad transmissions to specific boundaries (e.g., 64 bytes). If the EC responds with 12 bytes but the USB bridge pads the packet to 64 bytes with garbage data, the checksum validation will fail incorrectly.\n\n* **Suggestion:** Parse the header first, validate the `data_length` against the received size, and then run the checksum *strictly* over `sizeof(EcHostCommandResponse) + data_length` bytes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 85,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "6d644044c87bf5377358117e0ba7ceb2ddc3c5d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8bc3bbd_99526ba5",
        "filename": "util/egis/ec_comm.cc",
        "patchSetId": 33
      },
      "lineNbr": 85,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-05T17:53:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini suggested fix and test case:\n\n----\n\n### 1. Fix the payload parsing in `ec_comm.cc`\n\nOpen `util/egis/ec_comm.cc` and locate the `SendCommand` function. Find this block of code (around line 75):\n\n```cpp\n  if (actual_res.value() \u003c static_cast\u003cint\u003e(sizeof(EcHostCommandResponse))) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] EC response was too short to be valid.\");\n    return std::unexpected(EcError::kResponseTooShort);\n  }\n  resp_buf.resize(actual_res.value());\n\n  if (!VerifyResponseChecksum(resp_buf)) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] EC response checksum verification failed.\");\n    return std::unexpected(EcError::kInvalidChecksum);\n  }\n\n  auto hdr_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEcHostCommandResponse\u003e(resp_buf);\n  if (!hdr_res) {\n    return std::unexpected(EcError::kResponseTooShort);\n  }\n  EcHostCommandResponse resp_hdr \u003d hdr_res.value();\n\n```\n\nReplace that entire block with the new padding-safe logic:\n\n```cpp\n  size_t rx_size \u003d actual_res.value();\n  if (rx_size \u003c sizeof(EcHostCommandResponse)) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] EC response was too short to be valid.\");\n    return std::unexpected(EcError::kResponseTooShort);\n  }\n\n  auto resp_hdr \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEcHostCommandResponse\u003e(resp_buf).value();\n  uint16_t data_length \u003d FromLittleEndian(resp_hdr.data_length);\n  size_t exact_packet_size \u003d sizeof(EcHostCommandResponse) + data_length;\n\n  if (rx_size \u003c exact_packet_size) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] EC response data truncated. Claimed: {}, Actual: {}\",\n                 data_length, rx_size - sizeof(EcHostCommandResponse));\n    return std::unexpected(EcError::kResponseTooShort);\n  }\n\n  resp_buf.resize(exact_packet_size);\n\n  if (!VerifyResponseChecksum(resp_buf)) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] EC response checksum verification failed.\");\n    return std::unexpected(EcError::kInvalidChecksum);\n  }\n\n```\n\n### 2. Add the unit test in `ec_comm_test.cc`\n\nOpen `util/egis/ec_comm_test.cc` and scroll to the bottom of the file. Insert the new test block right before the closing namespaces (`}  // namespace`):\n\n```cpp\nTEST_F(EcCommTest, UsbPaddingIsIgnored) {\n  const std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e mock_payload \u003d {0x01, 0x02, 0x03};\n  auto packet \u003d MakeMockResponse(0, mock_payload);\n\n  // Simulate USB bulk endpoint padding (e.g., to a 64-byte frame boundary)\n  constexpr size_t kUsbPaddedSize \u003d 64;\n  packet.resize(kUsbPaddedSize, 0xAA); \n  \n  fake_usb_.PushDeviceResponse(packet);\n\n  auto result \u003d\n      ec_.SendCommand(std::to_underlying(EcCommandId::kEcCmdGetVersion), 1);\n\n  ASSERT_TRUE(result.has_value());\n  EXPECT_EQ(result.value(), mock_payload);\n}\n\n```",
      "parentUuid": "d0f9de23_c7edc97b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 85,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "6d644044c87bf5377358117e0ba7ceb2ddc3c5d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
